-- title:
--   Admissible small constants at q=3, tamely fixed
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Then there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ such that, writing $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, $A_0$ is henselian, its residue field is algebraically closed, and every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$; moreover $k_0$ is stable under every $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying $x \in A \iff \tau x \in A$ for all $x$; and for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ (the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup) with $\overline{\tau\pi/\pi} = 1$ fixes $k_0$ pointwise. Finally there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   This provides the field of "small constants" $k_0$ over which the local geometric constructions at $q$ may be carried out: a henselian discretely valued subfield with algebraically closed residue field, carrying all residues of $A$, stable under the decomposition group and fixed by the kernel of the tame character, together with the auxiliary prime $\ell$ and the roots of unity and uniformiser-like element needed for the level structures. It is the $q=3$ counterpart of the corresponding statement for $q \ge 5$, and is used in the construction of supersingular prolongations and charts on modular curves of full level in the $q=3$ case.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_admissible_smallConstants_tameFixed_of_eq_three.lean

